# ClangSharpPInvokeGenerator response file for spa/pod/filter.h.
#
# Its own pass because it needs the one setting the ABI pass switches off: these functions are
# `static inline` in the header and exported from no shared library, so they cannot be bound as
# P/Invokes - they have to be *translated*. `funcs-with-body` is what makes ClangSharp emit the
# bodies as C# instead of skipping them.
#
# Why this is worth generating rather than hand-porting: spa_pod_filter is pod intersection - match
# object properties by key, intersect choices (None/Enum/Range/Step/Flags) against fixed values and
# against each other, preserve DONT_FIXATE. Roughly 430 lines of fiddly logic where a subtle
# mistranslation produces a format negotiation that silently agrees on the wrong thing. Generated,
# it tracks upstream on the next bump instead of drifting.
#
# An exported node needs it: port_enum_params is handed the peer's format as a filter and must
# return the intersection, which is what upstream's export-source does on every iteration.

# No --file here on purpose: generate.sh passes the composite header absolutely. Naming it in both
# places makes a second root, and the relative one fails to parse with CXError_Failure - the same
# trap the constants pass hit.

# Only the filter header's own declarations. The pod types it operates on are already generated by
# the ABI pass into this same namespace, so they resolve without being re-emitted.
--traverse
/usr/include/spa-0.2/spa/pod/filter.h

--include-directory
/usr/include/pipewire-0.3
--include-directory
/usr/include/spa-0.2

# The ABI pass renames this enum, and the two passes have to agree or the generated filter refers
# to a type that exists under another name.
# Emitted into PipeWire.NET.Spa rather than .Interop, because the choice enum it switches on lives
# there and ClangSharp qualifies its `using static` with this pass's own namespace - so the two have
# to agree. The pod structs it takes come from .Interop via a using in the header.
# The ABI pass renames this enum; with both passes now in the same namespace, the remap is all that
# is needed for the generated switch to resolve.
--remap-type
spa_choice_type=SpaChoiceType

--namespace
PipeWire.NET.Spa

# Not "SpaPodFilter": a hand-written class of that name already exists in this namespace. The
# translated C is a distinct thing and says so.
--method-class-name
SpaPodFilterNative

--with-access-specifier
*=Internal

--generate
funcs-with-body
file-scoped-namespaces

--config
file=single
codegen=preview
types=unix

--output
src/PipeWire.NET/generated/SpaPodFilter.g.cs
